opam-version: "2.0"
name: "rocq-pi-leibniz"
version: "1.0.0"
synopsis:
  "Constructive pi for the Rocq constructive Cauchy reals with premise-free rational separation"
description: """
A constructive pi for the constructive Cauchy reals of the Rocq standard
library ([ConstructiveCauchyReals]), realized by the alternating Leibniz
series, with the strong irrationality separation theorem

  Theorem pi_leibniz_strong_irrational :
    forall a b : Q, b <> 0 -> CReal_appart pi_leibniz (inject_Q (a / b)).

together with its premise-free companion

  Theorem pi_leibniz_appart_all_Q :
    forall q : Q, CReal_appart pi_leibniz (inject_Q q).

pi is apart, in the sense of [CReal_appart], from every embedded rational
constant; the apartness witness comes with an explicit positive margin and
an explicit convergence modulus for the realizer.

Every witness is explicitly constructed and the statements are
[Set]-valued throughout, so the witnesses are extractable: the extracted
OCaml carries zero [Obj.magic].  Both main statements are premise-free
and closed under the global context ([Print Assumptions] reports
"Closed under the global context"; the [coqchk -o] assumption summary is
all-none).  Sample points run in the REPL with [vm_compute]: for
[q = 22 # 7] the escape-witness triple computes to
[(22 # 7, 5 # 8, 3%nat) : Q * Q * nat].

The content modules compile green on Rocq 9.1 locally and across the CI
matrix of the hosting standard-library submission (Alpine build and
Rocq 9.2 / 9.3 / master Nix bundles; 180/180 checks passed at the
submitted head), as an integral part of the standard-library tree.
"""
